==============================================================================
(1) THE THERMAL LAW AT THE CORPUS'S OWN FREQUENCY
==============================================================================
  T_c = tau m_e            = 177.099 keV      (tau = ln2/2)
  w_1 = (2/9) T_c          = 39.355 keV
  x_1 = hbar w_1 / k T_c   = 0.222222
  x_0 = x_1 / sqrt2        = 0.157135

  Bose occupancy of the charged mode at that x:
    n_bar = 1/(e^x - 1)    = 4.0185
  Equipartition is the n_bar >> 1 limit. At n_bar ~ 4 the classical form is an
  approximation, not an identity -- and the null is quoted as an identity.

  Q under the exact thermal law, with eps_D = 2 eps_S held exactly:
    rho^2 = (1/2) g(x_1)/g(x_0) = 0.501025429
    Q     = 0.667350286
    2/3   = 0.666666667
    miss  = 1025.4 ppm, against a claimed exactness of 6 ppm
    -> the correction is 171x LARGER than the agreement it must not disturb

==============================================================================
(2) HOW CLASSICAL WOULD THE MODES HAVE TO BE?
==============================================================================
  Q stays within 6 ppm of 2/3 only for x_1 <= 0.016971
  the corpus's x_1 is                                  0.222222
  so w_1 would have to be smaller by a factor          13.1
  i.e. w_1 <= 3.005 keV against the recorded 39.355 keV

         x_1      n_bar              Q   ppm from 2/3
  ------------------------------------------------------
    0.001000    999.500    0.666666681            0.0
    0.010000     99.501    0.666668056            2.1
    0.016971     58.426    0.666670667            6.0
    0.050000     19.504    0.666701383           52.1
    0.100000      9.508    0.666805463          208.2
    0.222222      4.019    0.667350286         1025.4
    0.500000      1.541    0.670081836         5122.8
    0.693147      1.000    0.673131624         9697.4

  The classical limit is EXACT and every finite x breaks it in the same direction --
  Q rises above 2/3, monotonically. There is no cancellation to hope for: the charged
  sector sits at the higher frequency, so it is always the more quantum of the two, and
  its power is always suppressed less than the classical formula says.

  Equivalently, holding Q = 2/3 exactly at the corpus's x_1 requires
    eps_D/eps_S = 2.004110  rather than 2 exactly,
    i.e. a = 2.9877 b  rather than a = 3b.
  So 'a = 3b' is the CLASSICAL statement of the null, not its exact statement, and the
  clean integer 3 is an artifact of the limit rather than a structural fact.

==============================================================================
(3) THE OCCUPANCY LOCK IS A FIFTH LAW -- AND IT IS NOT THERMAL
==============================================================================
  The lock does not use equipartition at all. Its argument is quantum and cold:
    N_0 = M w f_0^2 / hbar = 1        (the neutral mode carries one quantum)
    E_c = M w^2 R_c^2 = hbar w        (the charged PAIR sits in its ground state,
                                       2 dof x (1/2) hbar w)
  from which f_0^2 = R_c^2 = hbar/(M w) and the null follows with M and w cancelling.

  That cancellation is the lock's whole strength -- and it needs ONE w. The argument
  as recorded writes the same symbol in both lines. But the null it is explaining says
  the two sectors do NOT share a frequency:

    eps_1 = 2 eps_0   =>   w_1 = sqrt2 w_0

    neutral, one quantum at w_0 :  f_0^2 = hbar/(M w_0)  -> 1.000000  (hbar/M = 1)
    charged pair ground state    :  R_c^2 = hbar/(M w_1)  -> 0.707107
    R_c / M_c = (w_0/w_1)^(1/2)  = 0.840896   = 2^(-1/4)
    the null needs                 1.000000
    miss                           15.9%

  So the lock's derivation is frequency-degenerate: it delivers the null only if the
  neutral and charged sectors share w, and the stiffness reduction it is supposed to
  explain says they differ by sqrt2. Written with distinct frequencies the same three
  lines give 2^(-1/4) = 0.841, not 1.

  This is not fatal to the lock and it is not cosmetic. It is a NAMED condition the
  lock now owes: either the two sectors are degenerate at the moment the quanta are
  counted -- which is a statement about the freeze, before the stiffnesses split --
  or the lock's cancellation does not happen. The lock's own filter score (2 for 2,
  against 0 for 22 for the retired mechanisms) is untouched by this; what changes is
  that it has a specific, checkable debt instead of an unexamined step.

==============================================================================
(4) tau AND UNIT OCCUPANCY — AN EXACT IDENTITY, AND THE FORK IT OPENS
==============================================================================
  Sitting in the table above, at the last row: n_bar = 1 falls at x = ln2 exactly.
  The corpus's central constant is tau = ln2/2. So, as an identity in nothing but the
  Bose factor:

      n_bar = 1  <=>  e^x = 2  <=>  x = ln2  <=>  hbar w / kT = 2 tau

    check: n_bar(ln2) = 1.000000000000
           2 tau      = 0.693147180560      ln2 = 0.693147180560

  This is worth stating precisely because it is easy to over-read. It does NOT derive
  tau. It says that the SAME number the corpus reaches from -ln(rho) is the value of
  hbar w / 2kT at which a bosonic mode holds exactly one quantum -- which is the
  occupancy lock's premise, reached from the opposite side of the theory.

  It also sharpens the fork, because the two cannot both hold:
    unit occupancy needs   hbar w / kT_c = ln2      = 0.693147
    the corpus records     w_1 = (2/9) T_c         = 0.222222
    ratio                  (ln2)/(2/9) = 9 ln2 / 2 = 3.119162

    (That ratio is 9ln2/2 = 3.119162. It is NOT pi -- pi = 3.141593, off by 0.7%. Recorded so
     the near-miss is not chased later.)

  In frequency: unit occupancy puts w at 122.76 keV, the recorded w_1 is 39.36 keV.
  One of the two is wrong, or they refer to different modes. That is a bounded,
  answerable question, and it is the first time the two live arcs -- the tau modulus
  and the occupancy lock -- have been made to contradict each other on a number.

  AMENDED 2026-07-29 -- the ratio is NOT an independent contradiction.
  scripts/occupancy_frequency_keystone_identity.py shows 9ln2/2 = 9*tau = 6/c_K
  exactly, and that the tau CANCELS out of it (verified over a wide range of tau,
  max deviation 0.00e+00). So this ratio is the keystone c_K*tau = Q with the
  modulus divided out -- it was already implied the moment w_1/T_c was identified
  with arg b = Q/3, and it carries no information the keystone did not carry.
  Carry it as an INSTANCE of the c_K debt, not as its own open question: it is
  evidence against neither arc, and deriving c_K settles it automatically.
  The asymmetry still stands, though -- 'hbar w/kT = ln2' is a thermodynamic
  condition, while 'w_1/T_c = arg b' equates a frequency ratio with a phase, which
  is an identification rather than a derivation and is the step to examine first.

==============================================================================
VERDICT — THE LAW IS NARROWED, NOT YET FIXED
==============================================================================
  The thermal law cannot carry the null at the claimed exactness at the corpus's own
  frequency: it distorts Q by 1025 ppm against a 6 ppm budget. Two ways out,
  and they are both real statements rather than escapes:

    (a) the modes are far more classical than w_1 = (2/9) T_c implies (x_1 <=
        0.0170, a factor 13 smaller). Note that w_1 = (2/9)T_c is
        itself derived FROM Q = 2/3 via theta_B, so it is not an independent
        measurement and this route is not circular to take -- but it does mean the
        corpus currently has no independent handle on x_1 at all.

    (b) the delivery law is not thermal. The occupancy lock is the live alternative
        and it is a cold, quantum law -- which is the right CLASS for a 6e-6 claim,
        since an integer occupancy cannot drift while a thermal ratio can. Its debt
        is now named and it is a single condition.

  Either way the classical equipartition reading of the null is the one under pressure,
  and 'a = 3b' should be carried as its classical limit rather than as an exact
  structural relation.
